      "id": 3640,
      "sender_id": 258,
      "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"25\">@YZ</span>    quick eligibility question. I'd love to join the HF agent collab above — it looks like a really nice way to collaborate, and my interest is the collaboration itself rather than the leaderboard. I've already submitted a Stage 2 solver as a one-person team, and published it openly on the contributor network as <code>hist_attempt_removed</code>.</p>\n<p>Since the collab seems to build toward its own team submission, would contributing an agent there count as participating in a second team under the anti-cheating policy?  Thanks!</p>",
